@startuml Spring Courier - Diagrama de Sequência: Publicação de Notificações
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white

participant "Service" as Service
participant "Courier" as Courier
participant "NotificationRegistry" as NotificationRegistry
participant "EmailHandler" as EmailHandler
participant "CacheHandler" as CacheHandler
participant "LogHandler" as LogHandler
participant "EmailService" as EmailService
participant "CacheService" as CacheService
participant "LogService" as LogService

title Fluxo de Publicação de Notificações (Event Pattern)

== Evento de Domínio ==
Service -> Service: create product in database
activate Service
note right of Service
  Após uma operação bem-sucedida,
  o serviço publica um evento
end note

== Publicação Síncrona ==
Service -> Courier: publish(ProductCreatedEvent)
activate Courier

Courier -> NotificationRegistry: getHandlers(ProductCreatedEvent.class)
activate NotificationRegistry
NotificationRegistry --> Courier: List<NotificationHandler>\n[EmailHandler, CacheHandler, LogHandler]
deactivate NotificationRegistry

note right of Courier
  Todos os handlers registrados
  para o evento são executados
  sequencialmente
end note

== Execução do Handler 1 ==
Courier -> EmailHandler: handle(ProductCreatedEvent)
activate EmailHandler
EmailHandler -> EmailService: sendEmail(event.productId, event.name)
activate EmailService
EmailService --> EmailHandler: email sent
deactivate EmailService
EmailHandler --> Courier: void
deactivate EmailHandler

note right of EmailHandler
  Erros são capturados e logados,
  mas não interrompem a execução
  dos demais handlers
end note

== Execução do Handler 2 ==
Courier -> CacheHandler: handle(ProductCreatedEvent)
activate CacheHandler
CacheHandler -> CacheService: updateCache(event.productId)
activate CacheService
CacheService --> CacheHandler: cache updated
deactivate CacheService
CacheHandler --> Courier: void
deactivate CacheHandler

== Execução do Handler 3 ==
Courier -> LogHandler: handle(ProductCreatedEvent)
activate LogHandler
LogHandler -> LogService: logEvent(event)
activate LogService
LogService --> LogHandler: logged
deactivate LogService
LogHandler --> Courier: void
deactivate LogHandler

Courier --> Service: void
deactivate Courier

Service --> Service: continue workflow
deactivate Service

note right of Service
  O método publish() é síncrono,
  aguardando todos os handlers
end note

== Publicação Assíncrona (Alternativa) ==
Service -> Courier: publishAsync(ProductCreatedEvent)
activate Courier
activate Service

Courier -> Courier: CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> publish(event))
note right of Courier
  Execução assíncrona permite
  que o serviço continue sem
  aguardar os handlers
end note

Courier --> Service: CompletableFuture<Void>
deactivate Courier

Service --> Service: continue immediately
deactivate Service

note right of Service
  O serviço não aguarda a
  conclusão dos handlers
end note

@enduml
